    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nOn a successful owner create, a welcome notification is now enqueued via the `NOTIFY` logger, carrying the owner id and memberId.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New step function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NotifyWelcome.java`: gets the saved `Owner` via `@Val`, and emits `NOTIFY.info(\"Welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", ...)` on the logger named `NOTIFY` (modeled on the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` pattern).\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `notifyWelcome` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `audit` and `recordIdempotency`. It runs after `save` (so the id is assigned) and after `assignMemberId` (so the memberId is set).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreEnqueuesWelcome` \u2014 which asserts a `NOTIFY` line contains both the owner id and memberId \u2014 passes, as does the full suite. The captured output confirms it: `INFO NOTIFY - Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
